    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.65 from 7 h onward. Dilutions of the 18 h aliquot read much higher than 0.65 once scaled back up, so the reader is saturating. Scaled readings: 10x gave 0.251, or 2.51 equivalent. 40x gave 0.0552, or 2.21. 100x gave 0.0243, or 2.43. The scaled values are roughly consistent at about 2.2–2.5, and all are about 3.5 times the undiluted reading of 0.644. The 10x value may still be slightly compressed. The plateau therefore reflects reader non-linearity, not a stationary phase at that biomass."
